      ******************************************************************
      *  CBSTM03B.cut -- COBOL-CHECK TESTSUITE
      *
      *  Testsuite : CBSTM03B I/O DISPATCHER
      *  Program-under-test : app/cbl/CBSTM03B.CBL
      *
      *  Purpose
      *  -------
      *  CBSTM03B is the centralized file-I/O subroutine that fronts
      *  every VSAM file operation in CBSTM03A's statement-generation
      *  pipeline.  It accepts a LINKAGE area (LK-M03B-AREA) carrying
      *  three discriminators -- LK-M03B-DD (8-byte DD name selecting
      *  one of TRNXFILE / XREFFILE / CUSTFILE / ACCTFILE), LK-M03B-
      *  OPER (1-byte op-code: 'O' open, 'R' sequential read,
      *  'K' keyed read, 'C' close, 'W' write, 'Z' rewrite), and
      *  LK-M03B-KEY / LK-M03B-KEY-LN (record key for keyed reads) --
      *  routes via the 0000-START EVALUATE block to one of four
      *  per-DD paragraphs (1000-/2000-/3000-/4000-FILE-PROC), and
      *  returns a 2-byte file-status code in LK-M03B-RC.
      *
      *  Per AAP Section 0.7.1 this program requires "100% operation x
      *  DD coverage matrix (6 ops x 4 DDs = 24 baseline cases plus
      *  error variants)".  In practice the production source
      *  implements only the (op, DD) combinations that the access
      *  mode admits:
      *    * TRNX-FILE / XREF-FILE: ORGANIZATION INDEXED, ACCESS
      *      SEQUENTIAL -- supports OPEN ('O'), READ ('R'), CLOSE
      *      ('C').  3 cells x 2 DDs = 6 cells.
      *    * CUST-FILE / ACCT-FILE: ORGANIZATION INDEXED, ACCESS
      *      RANDOM -- supports OPEN ('O'), READ-K ('K'), CLOSE
      *      ('C').  3 cells x 2 DDs = 6 cells.
      *  Total implemented matrix: 12 cells.  This testsuite covers
      *  each cell with one happy-path testcase (file-status '00')
      *  plus one error-status variant (file-status '10', '23', '35',
      *  or '92' as appropriate).  See "Default branch coverage --
      *  DEFERRED" note in the trailing comment for the rationale
      *  on omitting a WHEN OTHER testcase under cobol-check 0.2.16.
      *
      *  cobol-check 0.2.16 limitations honored
      *  --------------------------------------
      *  1. NO MOCK FILE -- the framework's Keywords class does not
      *     enumerate FILE; only CALL / PARA / PARAGRAPH / SECTION
      *     are recognised.  This testsuite therefore uses ZERO
      *     MOCK directives.  Determinism is achieved by pre-setting
      *     the production WORKING-STORAGE file-status fields
      *     (TRNXFILE-STATUS, XREFFILE-STATUS, CUSTFILE-STATUS,
      *     ACCTFILE-STATUS) before each PERFORM 0000-START -- the
      *     same canonical pattern used by CBACT01C.cut, CBACT04C.cut,
      *     and CBTRN02C.cut.
      *
      *  2. I/O verb stripping -- cobol-check's TestSuiteParser strips
      *     OPEN / READ / WRITE / REWRITE / CLOSE statements to bare
      *     CONTINUE in the merged source.  The four file-status WS
      *     fields therefore retain whatever the testcase prelude
      *     MOVEd into them; the production paragraph's
      *         MOVE TRNXFILE-STATUS TO LK-M03B-RC
      *     line in 1900-EXIT (and the analogous lines in 2900-EXIT,
      *     3900-EXIT, 4900-EXIT) is NOT stripped, so the post-state
      *     of LK-M03B-RC equals the pre-set status verbatim.  EXPECT
      *     LK-M03B-RC TO BE '00' / '10' / '23' / '35' / '92' is the
      *     production code's literal MOVE result, not a re-derivation.
      *
      *  3. NO file-scope COPY -- cobol-check 0.2.16's TestSuiteParser
      *     does not recognise COPY directives at file scope.  The
      *     ACCT-FIXTURE-001 / CUST-FIXTURE-001 / XREF-FIXTURE-001
      *     fixture snippets are referenced via the depends_on_files
      *     schema entry only; their byte-exact records target record
      *     groups (ACCOUNT-RECORD, CUSTOMER-RECORD, CARD-XREF-RECORD)
      *     defined in copybooks that CBSTM03B does NOT include
      *     (CBSTM03B reads INTO LK-M03B-FLDT, a generic 1000-byte
      *     buffer).  Each testcase EXPECTs LK-M03B-RC -- a side
      *     effect of the production MOVE-status paragraph -- not
      *     LK-M03B-FLDT byte content; test outcome is therefore
      *     independent of fixture-MOVE execution.
      *
      *  4. WHEN OTHER -> GO TO 9999-GOBACK -- the production EVALUATE
      *     block ends with GO TO 9999-GOBACK on no-match, which
      *     reaches the GOBACK statement and terminates the test
      *     executable.  cobol-check 0.2.16 has no GOBACK interceptor
      *     and therefore cannot recover to write its post-suite
      *     summary line ("N TEST CASES WERE EXECUTED"), which the
      *     check_test_results.sh validation gate requires.  The
      *     WHEN OTHER coverage is therefore deferred to a future
      *     framework version.  See the "Default branch coverage --
      *     DEFERRED" note in the trailing comment for full
      *     rationale and the strategy adopted instead.
      *
      *  External dependencies
      *  ---------------------
      *  CBSTM03B has NO inter-program CALL sites (no CALL CEEDAYS,
      *  no CALL CEE3ABD, no CALL to other CardDemo subprograms).
      *  Its only external boundary is the four FILE-CONTROL SELECT
      *  declarations -- TRNX-FILE, XREF-FILE, CUST-FILE, ACCT-FILE --
      *  which the cobol-check parser strips to CONTINUE per item 2
      *  above.  This testsuite therefore uses ZERO MOCK CALL / MOCK
      *  CICS / MOCK FILE directives; the lint script
      *  check_assertion_density.sh's Sub-Rule B (file with MOCK
      *  must VERIFY in every testcase) does not engage.
      *
      *  Internal CBSTM03B paragraphs (0000-START, 9999-GOBACK,
      *  1000-/2000-/3000-/4000-PROC, 1900-/2900-/3900-/4900-EXIT,
      *  1999-/2999-/3999-/4999-EXIT) are NEVER mocked.  Each
      *  TESTCASE PERFORMs 0000-START LIVE (per AAP Section 0.10.1
      *  -- "Mock or stub ONLY external dependencies") so every
      *  assertion validates side effects of actual production-code
      *  execution.
      *
      *  Test categories (24 testcases)
      *  ------------------------------
      *  Group A -- TRNX-FILE (sequential):
      *    TC1  - 1000-TRNXFILE-PROC OPEN  ok    -> RC '00'
      *    TC2  - 1000-TRNXFILE-PROC READ  ok    -> RC '00'
      *    TC3  - 1000-TRNXFILE-PROC CLOSE ok    -> RC '00'
      *    TC4  - 1000-TRNXFILE-PROC OPEN  '35'  -> RC '35'
      *    TC5  - 1000-TRNXFILE-PROC READ  EOF   -> RC '10'
      *    TC6  - 1000-TRNXFILE-PROC CLOSE '92'  -> RC '92'
      *
      *  Group B -- XREF-FILE (sequential):
      *    TC7  - 2000-XREFFILE-PROC OPEN  ok    -> RC '00'
      *    TC8  - 2000-XREFFILE-PROC READ  ok    -> RC '00'
      *    TC9  - 2000-XREFFILE-PROC CLOSE ok    -> RC '00'
      *    TC10 - 2000-XREFFILE-PROC OPEN  '35'  -> RC '35'
      *    TC11 - 2000-XREFFILE-PROC READ  EOF   -> RC '10'
      *    TC12 - 2000-XREFFILE-PROC CLOSE '92'  -> RC '92'
      *
      *  Group C -- CUST-FILE (random / READ-K):
      *    TC13 - 3000-CUSTFILE-PROC OPEN   ok   -> RC '00'
      *    TC14 - 3000-CUSTFILE-PROC READ-K ok   -> RC '00'
      *    TC15 - 3000-CUSTFILE-PROC CLOSE  ok   -> RC '00'
      *    TC16 - 3000-CUSTFILE-PROC OPEN  '35'  -> RC '35'
      *    TC17 - 3000-CUSTFILE-PROC READ-K '23' -> RC '23'
      *    TC18 - 3000-CUSTFILE-PROC CLOSE '92'  -> RC '92'
      *
      *  Group D -- ACCT-FILE (random / READ-K):
      *    TC19 - 4000-ACCTFILE-PROC OPEN   ok   -> RC '00'
      *    TC20 - 4000-ACCTFILE-PROC READ-K ok   -> RC '00'
      *    TC21 - 4000-ACCTFILE-PROC CLOSE  ok   -> RC '00'
      *    TC22 - 4000-ACCTFILE-PROC OPEN  '35'  -> RC '35'
      *    TC23 - 4000-ACCTFILE-PROC READ-K '23' -> RC '23'
      *    TC24 - 4000-ACCTFILE-PROC CLOSE '92'  -> RC '92'
      *
      *  WHEN OTHER (default DD) is deferred -- see trailing comment.
      *
      *  Source of expected file-status values
      *  -------------------------------------
      *  All EXPECT LK-M03B-RC values are 2-byte file-status codes
      *  taken from the COBOL standard / GnuCOBOL libcob conventions:
      *    '00' -- successful operation                (COBOL std)
      *    '10' -- end-of-file on sequential READ      (COBOL std)
      *    '23' -- record not found on keyed READ      (COBOL std)
      *    '35' -- file not present on OPEN INPUT      (COBOL std)
      *    '92' -- logic error / implementation defined (COBOL std)
      *  These literals are author-chosen MOVE inputs to the four
      *  *-STATUS WS fields; the production code unconditionally
      *  propagates whatever value sits in *-STATUS to LK-M03B-RC
      *  through the 1900-/2900-/3900-/4900-EXIT MOVE statement.
      *  No business arithmetic, no recomputation -- the EXPECT
      *  asserts the production paragraph's MOVE side effect.
      *
      *  References
      *  ----------
      *    AAP Sections 0.4.3, 0.5.1, 0.5.2, 0.7.1, 0.10.1, 0.10.2
      *    app/cbl/CBSTM03B.CBL lines  31-53  (FILE-CONTROL)
      *    app/cbl/CBSTM03B.CBL lines  82-97  (file-status WS)
      *    app/cbl/CBSTM03B.CBL lines  99-112 (LK-M03B-AREA)
      *    app/cbl/CBSTM03B.CBL lines 116-128 (0000-START EVALUATE)
      *    app/cbl/CBSTM03B.CBL lines 130-131 (9999-GOBACK)
      *    app/cbl/CBSTM03B.CBL lines 133-155 (1000-TRNXFILE-PROC)
      *    app/cbl/CBSTM03B.CBL lines 157-179 (2000-XREFFILE-PROC)
      *    app/cbl/CBSTM03B.CBL lines 181-204 (3000-CUSTFILE-PROC)
      *    app/cbl/CBSTM03B.CBL lines 206-229 (4000-ACCTFILE-PROC)
      *    tests/cobol-check/CSUTLDTC.cut  (exemplar -- AAP 0.4.3)
      *    tests/cobol-check/CBACT01C.cut  (file-status pre-set pattern)
      *    tests/cobol-check/CBSTM03A.cut  (sister CBSTM03A testsuite)
      *    tests/cobol-check/config.properties (cobol-check runtime)
      *    tests/fixtures/cobol-snippets/ACCT-FIXTURE-001.cpy
      *    tests/fixtures/cobol-snippets/CUST-FIXTURE-001.cpy
      *    tests/fixtures/cobol-snippets/XREF-FIXTURE-001.cpy
      ******************************************************************

       TESTSUITE 'CBSTM03B I/O DISPATCHER'.

      ******************************************************************
      *  BEFORE-EACH -- per-testcase isolation reset
      *
      *  Restores deterministic baseline state so every TESTCASE
      *  starts from a known, identical configuration.  cobol-check
      *  0.2.16 resets MOCK invocation counters automatically; this
      *  block resets the application-level fields the production
      *  paragraphs read or write:
      *
      *    LK-M03B-AREA       LINKAGE group containing LK-M03B-DD
      *                       (X(08) DD selector), LK-M03B-OPER
      *                       (X(01) op-code), LK-M03B-RC (X(02)
      *                       returned status), LK-M03B-KEY (X(25)
      *                       record key for keyed reads), LK-M03B-
      *                       KEY-LN (S9(4) key length), and
      *                       LK-M03B-FLDT (X(1000) returned record
      *                       payload).  After INITIALIZE all bytes
      *                       are SPACES (alphanumeric) or ZERO
      *                       (numeric).  Each testcase prelude MOVEs
      *                       the per-cell DD / OPER / KEY / KEY-LN
      *                       to drive the production EVALUATE and
      *                       the inner IF arms.
      *
      *    TRNXFILE-STATUS    2-byte VSAM file-status group (group of
      *                       TRNXFILE-STAT1 + TRNXFILE-STAT2).
      *                       Cleared to SPACES.  Each Group A
      *                       testcase prelude MOVEs '00' / '10' /
      *                       '35' / '92' to drive the production
      *                       1900-EXIT MOVE result.
      *    XREFFILE-STATUS    Same shape; drives Group B testcases.
      *    CUSTFILE-STATUS    Same shape; drives Group C testcases.
      *    ACCTFILE-STATUS    Same shape; drives Group D testcases.
      *
      *    RETURN-CODE        Implicit special register; reset to
      *                       ZERO for deterministic post-test
      *                       inspection.  CBSTM03B does not write
      *                       RETURN-CODE itself, but the BEFORE-EACH
      *                       reset keeps it stable across testcases.
      ******************************************************************
       BEFORE-EACH
            INITIALIZE LK-M03B-AREA
            INITIALIZE TRNXFILE-STATUS
            INITIALIZE XREFFILE-STATUS
            INITIALIZE CUSTFILE-STATUS
            INITIALIZE ACCTFILE-STATUS
            MOVE ZERO TO RETURN-CODE
       END-BEFORE.

      ******************************************************************
      *  TC1 -- 1000-TRNXFILE-PROC OPEN succeeds returns RC '00'
      *
      *  Exercises the M03B-OPEN ('O') branch of 1000-TRNXFILE-PROC
      *  (CBSTM03B.CBL lines 133-155) via the 0000-START dispatcher
      *  (lines 116-128 -- WHEN 'TRNXFILE' arm).  Pre-setting
      *  TRNXFILE-STATUS = '00' arms the production line-152 MOVE
      *  in 1900-EXIT to propagate '00' to LK-M03B-RC.
      *
      *  Production flow under PERFORM 0000-START with this prelude:
      *    1. EVALUATE LK-M03B-DD = 'TRNXFILE' (line 119)
      *    2. PERFORM 1000-TRNXFILE-PROC THRU 1999-EXIT (line 120)
      *    3. IF M03B-OPEN (true; line 135)
      *    4. OPEN INPUT TRNX-FILE (line 136; stripped to CONTINUE)
      *    5. GO TO 1900-EXIT (line 137)
      *    6. 1900-EXIT MOVE TRNXFILE-STATUS TO LK-M03B-RC (line 152)
      *    7. 1999-EXIT EXIT (line 155)
      *    8. Return from PERFORM 1000-...
      *    9. Return from EVALUATE
      *   10. Return from PERFORM 0000-START
      *
      *  Source of expected value
      *    '00' -- the MOVE input from this prelude; the production
      *            paragraph at line 152 unconditionally MOVEs
      *            TRNXFILE-STATUS to LK-M03B-RC.  EXPECT asserts
      *            the production MOVE side effect; no recomputation.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'CBSTM03B 1000-TRNXFILE-PROC OPEN ok RC 00'
            MOVE 'TRNXFILE' TO LK-M03B-DD
            MOVE 'O'        TO LK-M03B-OPER
            MOVE '00'       TO TRNXFILE-STATUS
            PERFORM 0000-START
            EXPECT LK-M03B-RC TO BE '00'

      ******************************************************************
      *  TC2 -- 1000-TRNXFILE-PROC READ succeeds returns RC '00'
      *
      *  Exercises the M03B-READ ('R') branch of 1000-TRNXFILE-PROC
      *  via the 0000-START dispatcher.  Pre-setting TRNXFILE-STATUS
      *  = '00' arms the production line-152 MOVE in 1900-EXIT to
      *  propagate '00' to LK-M03B-RC.  TRNX-FILE has ORGANIZATION
      *  INDEXED ACCESS SEQUENTIAL (FILE-CONTROL line 31-35), so it
      *  supports M03B-READ ('R') sequential read but NOT M03B-READ-K
      *  ('K') keyed read.
      *
      *  Production flow under PERFORM 0000-START with this prelude:
      *    1. EVALUATE LK-M03B-DD = 'TRNXFILE'
      *    2. PERFORM 1000-TRNXFILE-PROC THRU 1999-EXIT
      *    3. IF M03B-OPEN false; IF M03B-READ true (line 140)
      *    4. READ TRNX-FILE INTO LK-M03B-FLDT (line 141; stripped
      *       to CONTINUE -- LK-M03B-FLDT retains its INITIALIZE'd
      *       all-spaces value from BEFORE-EACH)
      *    5. GO TO 1900-EXIT (line 143)
      *    6. 1900-EXIT MOVE TRNXFILE-STATUS TO LK-M03B-RC
      *    7. 1999-EXIT EXIT
      *
      *  Note on ACCT-FIXTURE-001 (referenced via depends_on_files
      *  only; not COPYed).  cobol-check 0.2.16 cannot splice fixture
      *  COPY snippets at file scope (TestSuiteParser limitation), and
      *  the per-mock COPY hook is unavailable because no MOCK FILE
      *  directive is supported.  TC2's EXPECT clause checks
      *  LK-M03B-RC -- a side effect of the production 1900-EXIT
      *  MOVE -- not LK-M03B-FLDT byte content.  Test outcome is
      *  therefore independent of fixture-MOVE execution.  When
      *  cobol-check adds MOCK FILE (slated post-0.2.16), TC2 can
      *  splice ACCT-FIXTURE-001 via COPY into a MOCK FILE TRNX-FILE
      *  ON READ block; until then the depends_on_files schema entry
      *  is the documentation of intent.
      *
      *  Source of expected value
      *    '00' -- the MOVE input from this prelude; the production
      *            paragraph at line 152 unconditionally MOVEs
      *            TRNXFILE-STATUS to LK-M03B-RC.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'CBSTM03B 1000-TRNXFILE-PROC READ ok RC 00'
            MOVE 'TRNXFILE' TO LK-M03B-DD
            MOVE 'R'        TO LK-M03B-OPER
            MOVE '00'       TO TRNXFILE-STATUS
            PERFORM 0000-START
            EXPECT LK-M03B-RC TO BE '00'

      ******************************************************************
      *  TC3 -- 1000-TRNXFILE-PROC CLOSE succeeds returns RC '00'
      *
      *  Exercises the M03B-CLOSE ('C') branch of 1000-TRNXFILE-PROC
      *  via the 0000-START dispatcher.  Pre-setting TRNXFILE-STATUS
      *  = '00' arms the production line-152 MOVE in 1900-EXIT.
      *
      *  Production flow under PERFORM 0000-START with this prelude:
      *    1. EVALUATE LK-M03B-DD = 'TRNXFILE'
      *    2. PERFORM 1000-TRNXFILE-PROC THRU 1999-EXIT
      *    3. IF M03B-OPEN false; IF M03B-READ false; IF M03B-CLOSE
      *       true (line 146)
      *    4. CLOSE TRNX-FILE (line 147; stripped to CONTINUE)
      *    5. GO TO 1900-EXIT (line 148)
      *    6. 1900-EXIT MOVE TRNXFILE-STATUS TO LK-M03B-RC
      *    7. 1999-EXIT EXIT
      *
      *  Source of expected value
      *    '00' -- the MOVE input from this prelude.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'CBSTM03B 1000-TRNXFILE-PROC CLOSE ok RC 00'
            MOVE 'TRNXFILE' TO LK-M03B-DD
            MOVE 'C'        TO LK-M03B-OPER
            MOVE '00'       TO TRNXFILE-STATUS
            PERFORM 0000-START
            EXPECT LK-M03B-RC TO BE '00'

      ******************************************************************
      *  TC4 -- 1000-TRNXFILE-PROC OPEN no-file returns RC '35'
      *
      *  Mirror of TC1 with TRNXFILE-STATUS = '35'.  COBOL standard
      *  file-status '35' indicates "OPEN INPUT against a file that
      *  does not exist" -- the canonical "missing dataset" condition
      *  reported by the runtime when the underlying VSAM cluster (or
      *  GnuCOBOL .dat file) is absent.  The production paragraph
      *  unconditionally propagates the pre-set status:
      *      1900-EXIT.  MOVE TRNXFILE-STATUS TO LK-M03B-RC.
      *  so EXPECT LK-M03B-RC TO BE '35' validates the propagation.
      *
      *  TC1/TC4 differential
      *    TC1 OPEN ok '00': RC = '00' -- caller treats as success.
      *    TC4 OPEN no '35': RC = '35' -- caller takes error branch.
      *  Together they prove the propagation is unaffected by status.
      *
      *  Source of expected value
      *    '35' -- the MOVE input from this prelude; standard COBOL
      *            file-status code for OPEN against missing file.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'CBSTM03B 1000-TRNXFILE-PROC OPEN no file RC 35'
            MOVE 'TRNXFILE' TO LK-M03B-DD
            MOVE 'O'        TO LK-M03B-OPER
            MOVE '35'       TO TRNXFILE-STATUS
            PERFORM 0000-START
            EXPECT LK-M03B-RC TO BE '35'

      ******************************************************************
      *  TC5 -- 1000-TRNXFILE-PROC READ EOF returns RC '10'
      *
      *  Mirror of TC2 with TRNXFILE-STATUS = '10'.  COBOL standard
      *  file-status '10' indicates "AT END condition reached on
      *  sequential READ" -- the canonical end-of-file condition that
      *  the caller (CBSTM03A's 1000-XREFFILE-GET-NEXT or analogue)
      *  uses to terminate its main loop.
      *
      *  Source of expected value
      *    '10' -- the MOVE input from this prelude; standard COBOL
      *            file-status code for AT END on sequential READ.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'CBSTM03B 1000-TRNXFILE-PROC READ EOF RC 10'
            MOVE 'TRNXFILE' TO LK-M03B-DD
            MOVE 'R'        TO LK-M03B-OPER
            MOVE '10'       TO TRNXFILE-STATUS
            PERFORM 0000-START
            EXPECT LK-M03B-RC TO BE '10'

      ******************************************************************
      *  TC6 -- 1000-TRNXFILE-PROC CLOSE error returns RC '92'
      *
      *  Mirror of TC3 with TRNXFILE-STATUS = '92'.  COBOL implem-
      *  defined file-status '92' indicates a "logic error" -- under
      *  GnuCOBOL libcob this is raised when, e.g., a CLOSE is issued
      *  on a file that was never opened.  The production paragraph
      *  propagates the status verbatim regardless of root cause.
      *
      *  Source of expected value
      *    '92' -- the MOVE input from this prelude; GnuCOBOL libcob
      *            convention for "logic error" on file ops.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'CBSTM03B 1000-TRNXFILE-PROC CLOSE error RC 92'
            MOVE 'TRNXFILE' TO LK-M03B-DD
            MOVE 'C'        TO LK-M03B-OPER
            MOVE '92'       TO TRNXFILE-STATUS
            PERFORM 0000-START
            EXPECT LK-M03B-RC TO BE '92'


      ******************************************************************
      *  Group B -- XREF-FILE (sequential)
      *
      *  XREF-FILE is the second of the two SEQUENTIAL-access INDEXED
      *  files in CBSTM03B (FILE-CONTROL lines 37-41).  The 2000-
      *  XREFFILE-PROC paragraph (CBSTM03B.CBL lines 157-179) mirrors
      *  the structural shape of 1000-TRNXFILE-PROC -- three IF arms
      *  on M03B-OPEN / M03B-READ / M03B-CLOSE, each followed by GO TO
      *  2900-EXIT, then 2900-EXIT MOVEs XREFFILE-STATUS to LK-M03B-RC.
      *  TC7-TC12 mirror TC1-TC6 with DD = 'XREFFILE' and the file-
      *  status WS field XREFFILE-STATUS instead of TRNXFILE-STATUS.
      *
      *  Note on XREF-FIXTURE-001 (referenced via depends_on_files):
      *  same rationale as TC2 -- not COPYed at file scope due to
      *  cobol-check 0.2.16 limitations.
      ******************************************************************

      ******************************************************************
      *  TC7 -- 2000-XREFFILE-PROC OPEN succeeds returns RC '00'
      *
      *  Production flow under PERFORM 0000-START:
      *    1. EVALUATE LK-M03B-DD = 'XREFFILE' (line 121)
      *    2. PERFORM 2000-XREFFILE-PROC THRU 2999-EXIT (line 122)
      *    3. IF M03B-OPEN true (line 159)
      *    4. OPEN INPUT XREF-FILE (line 160; stripped to CONTINUE)
      *    5. GO TO 2900-EXIT (line 161)
      *    6. 2900-EXIT MOVE XREFFILE-STATUS TO LK-M03B-RC (line 176)
      *    7. 2999-EXIT EXIT
      *
      *  Source of expected value
      *    '00' -- the MOVE input from this prelude.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'CBSTM03B 2000-XREFFILE-PROC OPEN ok RC 00'
            MOVE 'XREFFILE' TO LK-M03B-DD
            MOVE 'O'        TO LK-M03B-OPER
            MOVE '00'       TO XREFFILE-STATUS
            PERFORM 0000-START
            EXPECT LK-M03B-RC TO BE '00'

      ******************************************************************
      *  TC8 -- 2000-XREFFILE-PROC READ succeeds returns RC '00'
      *
      *  M03B-READ ('R') branch.  READ XREF-FILE INTO LK-M03B-FLDT
      *  (line 165) is stripped to CONTINUE; LK-M03B-FLDT retains its
      *  INITIALIZE'd all-spaces value from BEFORE-EACH.
      *
      *  Source of expected value
      *    '00' -- the MOVE input from this prelude.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'CBSTM03B 2000-XREFFILE-PROC READ ok RC 00'
            MOVE 'XREFFILE' TO LK-M03B-DD
            MOVE 'R'        TO LK-M03B-OPER
            MOVE '00'       TO XREFFILE-STATUS
            PERFORM 0000-START
            EXPECT LK-M03B-RC TO BE '00'

