      ******************************************************************
      *  TC17 -- 3000-CUSTFILE-PROC READ-K not-found returns RC '23'
      *
      *  Mirror of TC14 with CUSTFILE-STATUS = '23'.  COBOL standard
      *  file-status '23' indicates "record not found" on keyed READ
      *  against an INDEXED file -- the canonical condition for a
      *  RECORD KEY value that does not match any record in the
      *  cluster.  CBSTM03A's caller paragraphs treat this as a
      *  not-found indicator and proceed accordingly.
      *
      *  Source of expected value
      *    '23' -- the MOVE input from this prelude; standard COBOL
      *            file-status code for "record not found" on keyed
      *            READ.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'CBSTM03B 3000-CUSTFILE-PROC READ-K not found RC 23'
            MOVE 'CUSTFILE'  TO LK-M03B-DD
            MOVE 'K'         TO LK-M03B-OPER
            MOVE '999999999' TO LK-M03B-KEY (1:9)
            MOVE +9          TO LK-M03B-KEY-LN
            MOVE '23'        TO CUSTFILE-STATUS
            PERFORM 0000-START
            EXPECT LK-M03B-RC TO BE '23'

