      ******************************************************************
      *  End of testsuite CBSTM03B I/O DISPATCHER
      *
      *  Default branch (WHEN OTHER) coverage -- DEFERRED
      *  ------------------------------------------------
      *  The 0000-START EVALUATE WHEN OTHER arm (CBSTM03B.CBL lines
      *  127-128) executes
      *      WHEN OTHER
      *        GO TO 9999-GOBACK.
      *  followed by 9999-GOBACK paragraph
      *      9999-GOBACK.
      *          GOBACK.
      *  Reaching the GOBACK statement under cobol-check 0.2.16's
      *  -x (executable) compile mode terminates the merged test
      *  executable IMMEDIATELY -- the framework's post-suite summary
      *  paragraph (which writes the "N TEST CASES WERE EXECUTED"
      *  line that target/cobol-check/testResults.txt requires)
      *  cannot run after a production GOBACK.  This is an
      *  unrecoverable framework-level limitation; cobol-check has
      *  no GOBACK interceptor.  A WHEN OTHER testcase therefore
      *  cannot run alongside the 24 cell-matrix testcases without
      *  losing the summary line.
      *
      *  Coverage strategy adopted instead:
      *    * The four valid WHEN arms ('TRNXFILE', 'XREFFILE',
      *      'CUSTFILE', 'ACCTFILE') are each exercised by 6
      *      testcases (TC1-TC24).  This proves the EVALUATE
      *      block correctly dispatches to the per-DD paragraphs
      *      under all expected inputs.
      *    * The WHEN OTHER arm is documented as covered by gcov
      *      coverage exclusion (a known-uncoverable line under
      *      cobol-check 0.2.16) and by manual inspection of the
      *      production source.
      *    * Future work (post-cobol-check-0.2.16): when the
      *      framework adds GOBACK interception or supports a
      *      "no-op GOBACK" mode, a TC25 testcase can be added
      *      that PERFORMs 0000-START with LK-M03B-DD = 'BADFILE!'
      *      and EXPECTs LK-M03B-RC TO BE SPACES (the BEFORE-EACH
      *      INITIALIZE'd default; no per-DD paragraph runs so no
      *      *-STATUS propagates).
      *
      *  Coverage achieved
      *  -----------------
      *  TC1-TC24 collectively cover the 12-cell implemented operation
      *  x DD matrix:
      *    * Group A (TC1-TC6):   1000-TRNXFILE-PROC  (lines 133-155)
      *      OPEN/READ/CLOSE happy + error paths.
      *    * Group B (TC7-TC12):  2000-XREFFILE-PROC  (lines 157-179)
      *      OPEN/READ/CLOSE happy + error paths.
      *    * Group C (TC13-TC18): 3000-CUSTFILE-PROC  (lines 181-204)
      *      OPEN/READ-K/CLOSE happy + error paths.
      *    * Group D (TC19-TC24): 4000-ACCTFILE-PROC  (lines 206-229)
      *      OPEN/READ-K/CLOSE happy + error paths.
      *
      *  Every defined WHEN arm of the 0000-START EVALUATE block is
      *  exercised at least once across TC1-TC24.  Every IF arm of
      *  the four per-DD paragraphs (M03B-OPEN, M03B-READ /
      *  M03B-READ-K, M03B-CLOSE) is exercised at least once.  Every
      *  per-DD *900-EXIT MOVE *-STATUS TO LK-M03B-RC paragraph is
      *  exercised with at least three distinct file-status inputs
      *  ('00', '10' or '23' or '35', and '92').  This satisfies the
      *  AAP Section 0.7.1 per-program target for CBSTM03B ("100%
      *  operation x DD coverage matrix plus per-cell error
      *  variants") for every cell that the production access mode
      *  admits and is reachable under the cobol-check framework.
      *
      *  Validation gates
      *  ----------------
      *  This file is designed to pass all four lint gates under
      *  tests/lint/:
      *    * check_no_business_logic.sh -- contains zero arithmetic
      *      verbs (COMPUTE / MULTIPLY / DIVIDE / ADD / SUBTRACT)
      *      anywhere in the file.  No MOCK PARAGRAPH or MOCK SECTION
      *      directive targets any internal CBSTM03B paragraph.
      *    * check_no_production_redeclaration.sh -- no IDENTIFICATION
      *      DIVISION or PROGRAM-ID line for CBSTM03B (or any other
      *      production program).
      *    * check_assertion_density.sh -- every TESTCASE has at least
      *      one EXPECT clause; no MOCK directive is used in this
      *      file, so VERIFY is not required (Sub-Rule B does not
      *      engage).
      *    * check_isolation.sh -- BEFORE-EACH block declared with
      *      INITIALIZE on every WS field touched.
      ******************************************************************

